# Runs the system suite against Linux and macOS.
#
# `crossbyte.sys.System` dispatches to a different class per platform, and the
# only one CI ever compiled was the Windows implementation: the group that
# covers it runs from the native smoke suite, which is a Windows job. macOS
# therefore reported zero processors for as long as it has been supported,
# with nothing to catch it.
#
# Paired with ci/posix-crypto-tests.hxml, which runs on the same two runners.
-cp src
-cp tests
-lib utest
-main PosixSystemMain
--cpp export/ci-posix-system
# Names the OS, as extraParams.hxml does for `-lib crossbyte`. Built from
# `-cp src` without it, nothing defined `linux` or `mac`, and the classes
# this job exists to test compiled out of it.
--macro crossbyte._internal.macro.HostPlatform.define()
--macro crossbyte.test.SuiteCoverage.check()
